From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] system: choose startup capabilities with -capabilities

A startup capability is something a run must choose before the machine
exists: record (the run may record) and taint (shadow state reserved
before guest memory). There are none by default; everything else needs
no capability.

-capabilities record,taint chooses them. They are sealed at the start of
qemu_init, before option, module and plugin processing can run
constructors that depend on them: a prepass over the real option table
(so an option-looking argument of -append or -device is not an option)
finds the last -capabilities. An embedding may choose them first
(panda_configure_capabilities); a -capabilities must then repeat that
choice. error_init moves up so the prepass can report.

The policy (system/capabilities.c, in the overlay) is built here.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later AND MIT
Origin: new
---
 qemu-options.hx    | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 system/meson.build |  1 +
 system/vl.c        | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/qemu-options.hx b/qemu-options.hx
index 6d6fc98da4dea3fce29ca1557a78342ba5ccf94b..30f6bd3d4197fd95752be1677e09e5c741fefa38 100644
--- a/qemu-options.hx
+++ b/qemu-options.hx
@@ -5635,6 +5635,22 @@ SRST
         Argument passed to the plugin. (Can be given multiple times.)
 ERST
 
+DEF("capabilities", HAS_ARG, QEMU_OPTION_capabilities,
+    "-capabilities record,taint\n"
+    "                choose startup capabilities (default: none)\n",
+    QEMU_ARCH_ALL)
+SRST
+``-capabilities names``
+    Choose the startup capabilities, a comma-separated list: what a run must
+    decide before the machine exists. ``record``: the run may record; it
+    launches a recordable machine, and a recording can't start without it.
+    ``taint``: reserve taint's shadow state (TCG only). There are none by
+    default. Everything else (plugins, callbacks, guest hypercalls, fast
+    snapshots, loading a snapshot taken under another accelerator or clock)
+    needs no capability. Unknown names are errors; the last ``-capabilities``
+    wins.
+ERST
+
 DEF("module", HAS_ARG, QEMU_OPTION_module,
     "-module path    load a panda module (external boards, devices) from a\n"
     "                shared object built with the engine's SDK\n"
diff --git a/system/meson.build b/system/meson.build
index 1623762cc9463db4f76c56dea5f5ed6726660fe1..15a455aafbd66bb1ab523bcfd3c7277d38d9e894 100644
--- a/system/meson.build
+++ b/system/meson.build
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ system_ss.add(files(
 
